    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Form-upload version (n8n on server, files on your PC)\n\nn8n runs on the server, so it can't read your laptop's files. This version takes the HTML\n**through your browser** and hands the Excel back as a download \u2014 no server file access and\nno `N8N_RESTRICT_FILE_ACCESS_TO` needed.\n\n**How to use**\n1. Open the \"On form submission\" node and copy its form URL.\n   - Test URL: works while the canvas is open and you click **Execute workflow**.\n   - Production URL: works once the workflow is **Active**.\n2. In your browser, open that URL, pick your dashboard `.html`, and submit.\n3. The filtered Excel (Overdue tickets for your owners) downloads automatically.\n\n**Config**\n- `ownerList` \u2014 your 5 owners (prefilled). Edit in the Config node.\n\n**Notes**\n- Columns: Overdue Tickets, Ticket URL, Severity, Assignment, State, Summary (plain text;\n  a clickable `=HYPERLINK` needs the online/Graph version).\n- \"Normalize upload\" auto-detects the uploaded file's binary property, so the parser just\n  works regardless of the form field name.\n- Prefer it to run on the server against a file instead? Put the HTML on a network share the\n  server can reach (e.g. an SMB mount), add that path to `N8N_RESTRICT_FILE_ACCESS_TO`, and\n  use the earlier file-based workflow. That needs whoever administers the n8n server.\n",
        "height": 600,
        "width": 500,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "dcc7fe2e-f96b-472e-a1a3-469cd7e78282",
      "name": "Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        240,
        560
      ]
    }
